# Rule 1: Backend only — do not touch the frontend

The user works on the backend only. The frontend is off-limits.

## Never edit, create, delete or reformat
- `apps/console/**` (Next.js pages, components, API routes, `lib/`, `next.config.ts`, `tsconfig.json`, `package.json`)
- Frontend dependencies (never `pnpm --filter @moncha/console add|remove`)

## Allowed (backend)
- `apps/worker/**`
- `packages/**` (`db`, `domain`, `contracts`, `integrations`, `crawling`, `config`)
- Prisma schema/migrations (Neon **dev** branch only; never prod)

## If a backend change seems to need a frontend change
Stop and tell the user what the console would need. Do not make the change.
Keep shared contracts backward compatible so the console keeps working unchanged.

## Environment
- Backend env lives in `apps/worker/.env` (template: `apps/worker/.env.example`).
- `apps/worker/src/poller.ts` loads `apps/worker/.env` first; the repo-root `.env` only fills missing keys.
- Put new backend keys in `apps/worker/.env`. Do not edit the repo-root `.env` (the console reads it).
- Never print secret values; show keys only.
